<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=bicycle">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bicycle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1817">1817</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pedal cycle, Push-bike</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A bicycle is a pedal-driven, single-track vehicle with two wheels attached to a frame, one behind the other. Its first form, Karl von Drais’s two-wheeled running machine without pedals, was shown in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a> in 1817, and pedals on an enlarged front wheel were added in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the early 1860s. The upright safety bicycle has changed little since the first chain-driven model of around 1885, and it gave women unprecedented mobility. Ball bearings, pneumatic tyres, chain-driven sprockets and tension-spoked wheels were first invented for the bicycle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bicycle.jpg" alt="Bicycle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karen Roe from Bury St Edmunds, Suffolk, UK, United Kingdom · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1886_Starley_'Rover'_Safety_Cycle_British_Motor_Museum_09-2016_(29928044262).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1817</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Mannheim</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Karl von Drais</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Drais’s running machine had no pedals; they were added in France in the early 1860s.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/wheel">Wheel<span>before 4000 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/automobile">Automobile<span>1886</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=bicycle">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
